[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Apache Geode %%VERSION%% is installed in %%DATADIR%% (GEODE_HOME); its
shell is %%PREFIX%%/bin/gfsh.

To run a locator and a server on this host as services:

  sysrc geode_locator_enable=YES geode_server_enable=YES
  service geode_locator start
  service geode_server start
  gfsh -e "connect --locator=localhost[10334]" -e "list members"

Both services read %%ETCDIR%%/gemfire.properties; their working
directories, with logs and persistent data, are below %%GEODE_DBDIR%%.
Member names default to locator-<hostname> and server-<hostname>.  The
remaining settings, among them heap size, ports and bind addresses, are
described at the top of %%PREFIX%%/etc/rc.d/geode_locator and
%%PREFIX%%/etc/rc.d/geode_server.

The locator serves Pulse at http://localhost:7070/pulse and the
management REST API on the same port.  Neither requires a login until a
security manager is configured: set one before exposing the locator,
or its JMX (1099) and HTTP (7070) ports, beyond a trusted network.

Jars placed in %%DATADIR%%/extensions are added to the classpath of gfsh,
of the rc.d services and of the members gfsh starts; a running cluster
also takes application jars through "gfsh deploy".

Geode %%VERSION%% needs Java 17 or newer; set geode_*_java_home, or
JAVA_HOME for gfsh, to use a JDK other than %%JAVA_HOME%%.
EOM
}
]
